1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,000
This video you're watching may have come through a hose under the sea.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,650
Over 99% of data between continents goes through undersea cables, not satellites.

3
00:00:10,650 --> 00:00:14,550
In the deep sea, the cable is only as thick as a garden hose.

4
00:00:14,550 --> 00:00:19,400
Cut it open, and there are a few glass fibers as thin as hair in the middle.

5
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:24,150
Around them are layers of copper, steel wire, and plastic.

6
00:00:24,150 --> 00:00:28,100
Light travels inside these glass fibers and carries the data.

7
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:32,450
The biggest danger is not sharks. It's fishing nets and ship anchors.

8
00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:37,150
A few thin lines under the sea connect the whole world every day.
